# settings-bands: the real Ajustes window open over the main screen, then the
# firmware's own Bands action run from there.
#
# The path is the firmware's own: main_screen_action(ACTION_APP_BANDS), the
# dispatcher the app-menu Bands button (src/buttons.cpp -> make_app_btn("Bands")
# -> main_screen_start_app) and the Ajustes long-press list (`APP Bands`,
# src/dialog_settings.c) both reach. The owner's route is APP -> app pages ->
# Bands; the app-menu button is the one that did nothing.
#
# `dialog_bands` is an inert mock on the host (tools/ui_harness/mocks/
# mock_main_screen.c), so the Bands window itself is not rendered: this fixture
# measures the ROUTE. src/screens.c (scenario_settle) codifies what the route
# must leave behind — the Ajustes window closed and a dialog running — and stops
# the run if it does not, instead of capturing a green capture of another state.
#
# The radio state matches settings-home / home-usb-20m so the only difference is
# the windows and the route.
#
# Deterministic: the date/time fields read the harness' fixed clock, not the
# host's (tools/ui_harness/CMakeLists.txt links with `--wrap=time`).

name settings-bands
screen settings-bands

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
